# Delivery for the request form (api/request.ts). Without GMAIL_USER and
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD the endpoint validates a submission but returns 503 and
# delivers nothing, which is what a bare local checkout does.
GMAIL_USER=you@gmail.com
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=your_google_app_password
# Where the notification lands. Falls back to GMAIL_USER when unset.
REQUEST_TO_EMAIL=you@gmail.com

# --- Optional, and silently inactive when unset -----------------------------
# Both of the protections below exist in code and fall back quietly, so an
# unconfigured deployment looks healthy while providing neither. Set them in
# the production environment, not only here.

# Shared rate-limit store, so five attempts an hour holds across serverless
# instances instead of per warm instance. Any Upstash-compatible REST endpoint
# (Vercel KV or Upstash). Unset, the limit falls back to a module-level Map,
# which does not limit a caller who lands on a fresh instance each time.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# Salts the digest of the caller's address before it reaches that store, so a
# leak of the store is not a leak of who submitted a request. Unset, a default
# is used — per-deployment stable, but not secret.
REQUEST_RATE_SALT=

# Where a failed delivery is announced. A failed delivery is a lead that was
# typed and lost, and the function log is not somewhere anyone is watching.
# The payload carries the SMTP code and the source attribution only — never the
# business, idea, name or email. Unset, the failure is logged and nothing else.
REQUEST_ALERT_WEBHOOK=
